//! The four CDL styles against PyOpenColorIO 2.5.1 (`CDLTransform`, default CPU processor), ROADMAP
//! G7. `vfx_lut::cdl` is the stack's one CDL (vfx-color and the vfx-ocio processor call it), so
//! this is where OCIO parity is pinned. The cases cover both of OCIO's CPU paths: power (1,1,1)
//! (the optimizer's matrix form: no power, saturation exact at 1) and any other power (the
//! renderer: SSE power on every channel, `x^1` included, saturation always), plus parameters below
//! OCIO's reciprocal floor of 0.01 (`tiny_slope`) and inputs outside [0, 1].
//!
//! Generated by `scratchpad/g7` from PyOpenColorIO 2.5.1; values printed with `%.9g`.

